<title>SWEDEN: SKF says Q1 profit falls 38 pct.</title>
<headline>SKF says Q1 profit falls 38 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish bearings manufacturer SKF on Tuesday reported its earnings for the three months ending March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		    501 vs   811</p>
<p> Group sales				 8,864 vs 8,881</p>
<p> Cost of goods sold			6,510 vs 6,343</p>
<p> Selling and admin expenses	    1,649 vs 1,668</p>
<p> Other op income/expense net   CHARGE   10 vs    25 CREDIT</p>
<p> Operating income			    695 vs   895</p>
<p> Financial items-net	     CHARGE  194 vs    84 CHARGE</p>
<p> Tax					     215 vs   290</p>
<p> Income after tax			    286 vs   521</p>
<p> Minorities			     CREDIT 3 vs     2 CHARGE</p>
<p> Net income				    289 vs   519</p>
<p> Earnings per share (SKR)		 2.60 vs  4.60</p>
<p>NOTE -- A Reuter poll found analysts expected SKF to report a Q1 profit after financial items of 651 million crowns.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
